\ port/lab/jit.4 - loaded first on a design with the JIT gene (its Makefile's -DX_JIT=1).
\
\ Such a design gives every colon word a header, [JIT][four bytes]: the
\ body's length with the top bit set until the word's first call, then the
\ native code's offset (forth-vm-evolution's forth/cv8t-jit.4, engine/jit.c).
\ The words the build runs are translated as it runs them, so an image saved
\ from it would carry offsets into the building process's code buffer - and
\ crash. This ; keeps each header's first value, and save.4 puts them back
\ in the saved copy, so the saved image starts as an unrun one.

8192 CONSTANT JH-MAX
VARIABLE JH-TAB   \ pairs: a header's length field, its value - allocated, so not saved
JH-MAX 2 * CELLS ALLOCATE DROP JH-TAB !
VARIABLE JH-N   0 JH-N !
: JH@ ( a --- u )   \ the four bytes, little end first
  DUP C@  OVER 1 + C@ 8 LSHIFT OR  OVER 2 + C@ 16 LSHIFT OR  SWAP 3 + C@ 24 LSHIFT OR ;
: ; ( --- )
  JIT-AT @ >R  POSTPONE ;  R>
  ?DUP IF JH-TAB @ IF                             \ the build's: JH-TAB is 0 after boot
    JH-N @ JH-MAX < IF
      DUP JH-TAB @ JH-N @ 2 * CELLS + !  JH@ JH-TAB @ JH-N @ 2 * 1 + CELLS + !  JH-N @ 1 + JH-N !
    ELSE DROP THEN
  ELSE 4 0 DO 0 OVER I + C! LOOP DROP THEN THEN ; IMMEDIATE
\ After boot a word - a forth command's - is left to the interpreter: its
\ header 0, as the JIT leaves a word it refused. The JIT's THROW cannot
\ unwind native code, and a forth command's words ABORT and THROW to the
\ command's CATCH (compile.4's depth tells more).
VARIABLE PRE-SAVE-XT   \ save.4 runs it on the copy: ( copy-of --- ) with an address converter
: JH-RESTORE ( xt --- )   \ xt: ( live-addr --- copy-addr )
  JH-N @ 0 ?DO
    JH-TAB @ I 2 * CELLS + @ OVER EXECUTE          ( xt copy )
    JH-TAB @ I 2 * 1 + CELLS + @ SWAP              ( xt v copy )
    4 0 DO 2DUP C! SWAP 8 RSHIFT SWAP 1 + LOOP 2DROP
  LOOP DROP ;

\ The kernel's own words, on a design with the gene jitimg: the converter
\ gave them headers too, and the build runs some of them. Their first
\ values are in the design's image file, which build.sh names here first.
VARIABLE JO-BUF   0 JO-BUF !     \ the original image's body
VARIABLE JO-LEN   0 JO-LEN !
VARIABLE JX
: JIT-PRISTINE ( c-addr u hdrlen --- )
  >R R/O OPEN-FILE ABORT" jit.4: cannot open the design's image" >R
  131072 ALLOCATE ABORT" jit.4: no memory" JO-BUF !
  JO-BUF @ 131072 R@ READ-FILE ABORT" jit.4: cannot read the design's image"
  R> CLOSE-FILE DROP
  R> DUP JO-BUF +!  - JO-LEN ! ;
: JH-KERNEL ( xt --- )   \ xt: ( live-addr --- copy-addr )
  JX !  JO-BUF @ 0= IF EXIT THEN
  JO-LEN @ 5 - 0 ?DO
    JO-BUF @ I + C@ JIT-OP = IF JO-BUF @ I + 4 + C@ 128 AND IF
      START @ I + JX @ EXECUTE                     ( copy )
      DUP C@ JIT-OP = IF  JO-BUF @ I + 1 + SWAP 1 + 4 MOVE  ELSE DROP THEN
    THEN THEN
  LOOP ;
: JIT-UNRUN ( xt --- )
  DUP JH-KERNEL  DUP JH-RESTORE
  \ the saved image's pointers into this process's memory: 0, so a word
  \ a forth command defines after boot records nothing
  DUP JH-TAB SWAP EXECUTE 0 SWAP !  JO-BUF SWAP EXECUTE 0 SWAP ! ;
' JIT-UNRUN PRE-SAVE-XT !
\ JIT-NEVER: the word just defined is saved as one the JIT refused - left
\ to the interpreter (save.4's PORT-BOOT: the JIT translates a word's
\ callees with it, and before RELOCATE has run their literals are wrong)
: JIT-NEVER ( --- )  JH-N @ IF  0 JH-TAB @ JH-N @ 1 - 2 * 1 + CELLS + !  THEN ;
